<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6050" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caenīna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καινινη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small but very
				ancient town in Latium</i>, <i>near Rome</i>, now
				<i>Ciano</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 68</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caenīnensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of
				Cœnina</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">SACERDOTIVM,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 436, 5</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caenīnenses</span></b> , ium,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of
				Cœnina</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 9, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 10, 2</span></i> and 3; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
				135</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caenīnus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of
			Cœnina</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arx,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 10, 9: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acron,</span>”
				<i>king of the Cœninenses</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 10, 7; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen = Caeninenses,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 10, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
